<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Zeta under the Crnojevići</h1><p class="st-meta">1451 CE – 1496 CE (approx.) · capital Cetinje</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Last free Serbian Orthodox principality of the 15th-century Balkans, where Ivan Crnojević founded Cetinje and his son set up the first South Slav printing press.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsic-noble-family">Balšić</a> lords and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-despotate">Serbian Despotate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crnojevic-noble-family">Crnojević</a> family took the lead in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-crnojevic">Stefan Crnojević</a>, ruling from around 1451, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a>, holding the territory around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-skadar">Lake Skadar</a> and the highlands behind the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-kotor">Bay of Kotor</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The principality was a confederation of mountain clans led by a hereditary lord who balanced Venetian alliance against Ottoman pressure. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-crnojevic">Ivan Crnojević</a> moved his seat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zabljak-crnojevica">Žabljak</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetinje">Cetinje</a> in 1482 and founded a monastery there in 1484. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durad-crnojevic">Đurađ</a> opened a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press that produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetinje-octoechos">Oktoih</a> in 1494, among the first Cyrillic books printed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Ottoman pressure forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durad-crnojevic">Đurađ Crnojević</a> to flee to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1496, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a> was absorbed into the Ottoman sanjak of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Scutari</a>. Leadership of the highlands passed to the metropolitans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetinje">Cetinje</a>, laying the ground for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-montenegro">Prince-Bishopric of Montenegro</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/zeta-under-the-crnojevici.jpg" alt="Zeta under the Crnojevići" width="320" height="185"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Zeta.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1451 CE – 1496 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cetinje</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Stefan Crnojević, Ivan Crnojević, Đurađ Crnojević</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Serbian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Principality of Zeta (Crnojević), Crnojević Zeta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1474&amp;focus=zeta-under-the-crnojevici" aria-label="Zeta under the Crnojevići on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5139 670 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Zeta under the Crnojevići lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5459 926L5488 850M5459 926L5293 831M5459 926L5709 970M5459 926L5459 926"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5488 850h0M5293 831h0M5709 970h0M5459 926h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5459 926h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5459 926h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cetinje. <a href="/atlas?year=1474&amp;focus=zeta-under-the-crnojevici">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside><